[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"Submitters using DistSSHKitQueue or julia -m DistSSHKitQueue submit go …. Queue code using DistSSHKit. Job files for Kit go still do not import DistSSHKit.\n\nPrefer julia -m DistSSHKitQueue. From a client: qhost:HOST (not --hosts). Default hop: DISTSSHKITQUEUE_HOST. add-host / remove-host write config hosts on the queue host (Kit tokens parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). Do not restart serve; the next submit re-reads the file. list-host is read-only (not Kit --hosts). size is DistSSHKit size on the queue host. cancel of :running uses the Kit output dir (allocated at start if submit omitted --output-dir). CLI submit uses follow_config; library submit! uses Queue(; allowed=…) unless follow_config=true. Config: ~/.distsshkitqueue/config.toml.\n\nLibrary surface:","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.DistSSHKitQueue","page":"API","text":"DistSSHKitQueue — FIFO waiter for DistSSHKit (go / drive).\n\nPackage entry: exports, includes, main (@main on Julia 1.12+). FIFO: src/DistSSHKitQueue/. Client CLI: src/client/. Queue host CLI: src/qhost/. Waiter runs DistSSHKit execute!(...; detached=true). --project=<queue-env> loads this package; the job tree is job_project(). Config: ~/.distsshkitqueue/config.toml.\n\nConcept and design notes: README.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.DistSSHKitQueue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.Queue","page":"API","text":"FIFO table: one DistSSHKit job at a time. Placement tokens are Kit's, not a Queue ceiling.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.Queue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.Job","page":"API","text":"One table row. hosts are DistSSHKit 0.4 tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). kwargs is an opaque bag for DistSSHKit execute! (project is the job tree).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.Job"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.submit!","page":"API","text":"Enqueue. kind=:go or :drive (DistSSHKit execute!).\n\nhosts must be DistSSHKit 0.4 placement tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). Missing project uses job_project() (cwd / DISTRIBUTED_PROJECT_ROOT), not the waiter env (enable --queue-env / Julia --project= that loaded Queue). Same verb as CLI submit.\n\nq.allowed is the inventory (Queue(; allowed=…)), names plus optional max :N. It does not read config.toml. CLI submit uses Queue(; follow_config=true) so each enqueue re-reads hosts without restarting serve. step! does not drop :queued rows when a name is later removed, and does not stop a Kit job that is already :running.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.submit!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.cancel!","page":"API","text":"Cancel :queued, or :running via DistSSHKit terminate_run! when the Kit output dir is known.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.cancel!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHKitQueue.serve!","page":"API","text":"Load store (stale :running → :failed), then step! until interrupt. Ctrl-C stops the waiter, not Kit.\n\nA second serve on the same store prints Already running and returns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.serve!"},{"category":"section","location":"#DistSSHKitQueue.jl","page":"Introduction","text":"warning: Under construction. Do not use this.\n\n\nSmall-lab job queue on DistSSHKit.jl.\n\nDistSSHKit runs one job (go / drive). DistSSHKitQueue is a FIFO waiter in front of it: one queue host holds the table and the waiter; clients enqueue, list, watch, and cancel.\n\nNot on General yet. Julia 1.12+, DistSSHKit 0.4.1+. Placement tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]) stay DistSSHKit's — see the kit docs. Concept diagram and the full verb table: README.","title":"DistSSHKitQueue.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Client","page":"Introduction","text":"From the job directory. qhost:HOST names the queue host (like Kit child:NAME). One lab: export DISTSSHKITQUEUE_HOST=… and omit qhost: (the token still wins). --hosts / --julia stay on Kit go / drive.\n\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue --version\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST list-host\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST size\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST submit go child:host1:4 SCRIPT.jl\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST status -q\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST watch\njulia --project=. -m DistSSHKitQueue qhost:HOST cancel <id>\n\nsubmit starts a waiter on the queue host if none is running. status / watch print that qhost (or local (hostname)). There is no --via. watch is a live table (Ctrl-C); it does not stop the waiter.","title":"Client"},{"category":"section","location":"#Queue-host","page":"Introduction","text":"Always-on box (not a sleeping laptop). setup / serve / enable / disable / add-host / remove-host refuse qhost:.\n\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue setup\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue add-host parent child:host1\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue enable --queue-env ~/.distsshkitqueue/env\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue serve\njulia -m DistSSHKitQueue teardown -y\n\n--queue-env is the env that loads Queue in the OS unit, not Julia --project= / the job tree. teardown confirms like DistSSHKit (DISTSSHKIT_YES). The waiter calls DistSSHKit execute!(…; detached=true, job_id=…).","title":"Queue host"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Introduction","text":"From a checkout:\n\npkg> dev /path/to/DistSSHKitQueue.jl\n\nNeeds DistSSHKit 0.4.1+ from General (do not Pkg.develop Kit for ordinary Queue work), Julia 1.12+, plus ssh / rsync / git as in DistSSHKit.","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contributing","page":"Introduction","text":"Bugs and features: Issues. See CONTRIBUTING.md.","title":"Contributing"}]
